{{also|takk fyri}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|is|takk|fyrir|t1=thanks|t2=for}}, literally meaning "thanks for ...". Cognate with {{cog|fo|takk fyri}}.

===Interjection===
{{head|is|interjection}}

# {{lb|is|with accusative}} [[thank you]], [[thanks]]

====Usage notes====
* The interjection ''{{l|is|takk||thanks}}'' (borrowed from [[w:Danish|Danish]] ''{{l|da|tak}}'', from {{der|is|non|þǫkk}}) is largely interchangeable with ''{{l|is|þökk}}'', itself inhereted directly from Old Norse. ''Takk'' is rather informal, while ''þökk'' can be considered old-fashioned.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|is|takk}}
* {{l|is|þökk}}
* {{l|is|þökk fyrir}}
* {{l|is|þakka þér}} {{qualifier|singular}}; {{l|is|þakka yður}} {{qualifier|singular, formal; rare}} 
* {{l|is|þakka þér fyrir}} {{qualifier|singular}}; {{l|is|þakka yður fyrir}} {{qualifier|singular, formal; rare}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í dag||thanks for today}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í gær||thanks for yesterday}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í kvöld||thanks for tonight}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir mig}} (“thanks for myself”, commonly said to a host for having been received as a guest; both after dining and when departing)
* {{l|is|takk fyrir síðast}}, {{l|is|takk fyrir seinast||thanks for last time}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|þakka||to thank}}
* {{l|is|takk kærlega||thank you ''dearly''; thank you very much}}
* {{l|is|kærar þakkir||''dear'' thanks; thank you very much}}
* {{l|is|þúsund þakkir||thousand thanks}}

